{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791064247,"nonce":"602dwOX6b0KYjbn8HNlYHTyj004=","title":"A cargo build of caribou does not stage libhl beside the binary","message":"A Haxe program with an HDLL beside it runs through the shared libhl image, which caribou looks for beside its own executable (caribou-ash program.rs install_into_sibling_runtime). The nightly package puts libash_std.dylib, libhl.dylib (id @executable_path/libhl.dylib) and a libhl.1.dylib link there (scripts/package_nightly.sh), but a plain cargo build of target/\u003cprofile\u003e/caribou does not, and caribou then fails with \"this build of ash_core carries no runtime (the embedded-runtime feature is off)\". On 2026-10-03 the release binary was staged by hand for ashui (cp libash_std.dylib libhl.dylib, install_name_tool -id, codesign, ln -s libhl.1.dylib). Ash's own command does this in its build script (ash_cli/build.rs keeps a compatibility-named copy beside the executable); caribou-driver's build should do the same for the caribou binary, from the ash_std its own build produces.","files":null}]}